// fourWithHubFourBridges.recipe.jsonc — PHASE 5 DELIVERABLE RECIPE, hub kit role migration.
// AMBER_ARROW (Phase 5 builder), 2026-08-29, under RULING FJ-P5-1 (supervisor FROZEN_JOURNEY).
//
// fourWithHub-baseline PLUS the four bridge plugins that can coexist in ONE manifest. It is the
// recipe behind the DEV_ verification graph Phase 8 promotes by RENAME under GNC-001. It is a DEV_
// and it stays one until a goldEvalCheck PASS and the supervisor's live verification say otherwise.
//
// ── WHY FOUR BRIDGES AND NOT FIVE, MEASURED RATHER THAN INHERITED ──────────────────────────────
// A relationship block's subject is composed by vocabulary.js relationshipSubject as
//     <hubStandard>@<hubVersion> _rel_ <sourceStandard>@<sourceVersion> <producerSuffix>
// and RELATIONSHIP_PRODUCER_SUFFIX (vocabulary.js) is a three-row DATA map, not a conditional:
//     authored -> '_exact'   inferred -> '_close'   structural -> '_struct'
// The subject carries NO bridge name today; adding one is Phase 7's job. So two plugins collide
// only when they share BOTH a standard pair AND a producerKind. Measured from the five plugins'
// own declarations on 2026-08-29:
//     sifCedsStandardPlugin            sif         authored  -> ceds@..._rel_sif@..._exact
//     edfiCedsCrosswalkPlugin          edfi        authored  -> ceds@..._rel_edfi@..._exact
//     edfiCedsDerivedPlugin            edfi        inferred  -> ceds@..._rel_edfi@..._close
//     pescCedsDerivedPlugin            pesc260805  inferred  -> ceds@..._rel_pesc260805@..._close
//     pescOptionSetCedsDerivedPlugin   pesc260805  inferred  -> ceds@..._rel_pesc260805@..._close
// The ONLY colliding pair is PESC's two tiers. That IS ruling P2-R5 and it is narrower than the
// campaign prose had it: ED-FI'S TWO PLUGINS DO NOT COLLIDE, because a different producerKind
// gives them a different suffix and therefore a different subject. The four below compose FOUR
// DISTINCT subjects.
//
// ⚠ pescOptionSetCedsDerivedPlugin IS DELIBERATELY ABSENT, AND ITS ABSENCE IS A RECORDED DECISION
// RATHER THAN AN OVERSIGHT. It collides with pescCedsDerivedPlugin on the subject above and cannot
// share a manifest with it until Phase 7 puts the bridge name into relationshipSubject. It is NOT
// dropped and NOT out of scope: the plugin is shipped, validated and censused. The property tier is
// the one named here because it is the tier the whole P0/P0b measurement chain describes — a reason,
// not a ranking.
//
// ── HOW THIS RECIPE MUST BE RUN, AND WHY A PLAIN BUILD WOULD LIE ───────────────────────────────
// A PLAIN BUILD ASKS NO JUDGE. build.js resolveInferenceConfig mints a judge only when the
// --rebridge scope is ACTIVE; with an empty scope a build MATERIALIZES whatever frozen decision
// blocks the store already holds. Against a store carrying the CERTIFIED real-judge blocks, running
// this recipe without --rebridge would re-materialise those and report their numbers as though these
// bridges had been exercised — a check indistinguishable from a check that never ran.
// And with an ACTIVE --rebridge and no --useDebugJudge, the REAL Anthropic reranker is minted and
// Opus credit is spent, which this campaign forbids (SPEC section 6).
// Therefore, both flags, always:
//     --rebridge=all --useDebugJudge
// --useDebugJudge with no active scope is refused BY NAME, and so is --useDebugJudge alongside an
// injected llmClient. BOTH REFUSALS ARE READ FROM build.js AND WERE NOT OBSERVED RED by this phase —
// said plainly rather than left to read as though they had been exercised. DEFAULT_RULE is 'first', so every decision block header reads judgeKind
// 'debug:first' — the discriminator that separates this graph from a real-judge one. THE BRIDGE
// EDGE COUNTS THIS PRODUCES ARE NOT BYTE-ANCHORED, because a debug judge is not a judgement; only
// the AUTHORED and STANDARD-DECLARED portions are deterministic and comparable to the anchors.
//
// THREE STANDARDS ARE REUSED; SIF IS RE-FORGED, AND THAT IS NOT A DEFECT. Intended with
// --reuseForgedBlocks=true against a store whose four bases have already been certified, so the
// bridges run against exactly the blocks the entry gate vouched for.
// CORRECTED 2026-08-29 AFTER THE PHASE 5 REVIEW (finding F1) — the earlier wording here read
// "STANDARDS ARE REUSED, NOT RE-FORGED ... no forge cost is paid twice" and that is FALSE FOR SIF.
// MEASURED MECHANISM: reuse resolves a stored block by NAME, and forger.getVersionStamp will only
// name a version it can answer WITHOUT parsing the source — forger.js:373 refuses unless
// versionSource is 'provenance-file'. ceds (14.0.0.0), edfi (5.2.0) and pesc260805 (aggregate-01)
// each declare a publishedVersion in their standardSourceLocation and are reused. SIF's
// standardSourceLocation HONESTLY DECLARES publishedVersion: unknown, because the SIF
// implementation-spec TSV records no version at all — so the stamp cannot be 'provenance-file'
// and the caller MUST FORGE. SIF is therefore RE-FORGED on every reuse run, this one included.
// MEASURED HARMLESS HERE AND NOT ASSUMED SO: the re-forge produced the SAME content address
// d393b040..., so the bridges ran against the certified block; all 212 embedding batches were
// cache-served (0 distinct miss on every one), so no Voyage credit was spent. The cost is wall
// clock only, ~70 s of forge plus one scratch container.
// ⚠ THE STANDING HAZARD, NAMED RATHER THAN FIXED: because reuse resolves by NAME, if the SIF
// source or its forge moves between runs the re-forge lands under the SAME subject with a
// DIFFERENT id and nothing refuses. PESC had the same shape until Phase 4 gave it a
// standardSourceLocation (FJ-P4-7). Giving SIF an aggregate version token would close it, but it
// would RE-KEY the SIF block and every id downstream of it — a naming DECISION, not a bug fix.
// DOCKETED (FJ-P5-3); deliberately not done here.
//
// roundTripStage is ON: -goldEvalCheck REFUSES a run whose stage did not run (doctrine 7.4), and an
// acceptance recipe declares it (fourWithHub-baseline precedent).
//
// MEASURED 2026-08-29, AND THE NEXT PERSON TO RUN THIS RECIPE WILL MEET IT: A BUILD FROM THIS RECIPE
// CANNOT REACH A goldEvalCheck PASS, BY DESIGN, AND IT REFUSES TWICE FOR TWO DIFFERENT REASONS.
//   --buildLogDirPath alone -> REFUSED: 'the recipe DECLARES 4 bridge(s); mapping edges UNCERTIFIED
//     ... a bridged build never certifies on the forge round trip alone'. This is a SCOPE refusal.
//   plus --manifestRefId    -> the bridge sibling RUNS and REFUSES four times: each relationship block
//     'carries N edge(s) with provenanceTier invalid-debug ... a DEBUG-JUDGE block never reaches a
//     certified graph (Profile v1.0.6 4.6, RULING R5); re-judge with the real judge before promotion'.
//     This is a CONTENT refusal. 5,163 edges named across the four blocks.
// THE PAIR IS NOT REDUNDANT: the first says the question cannot certify a bridged build, the second
// says the answer would be invalid-debug. Either alone would let a run report something comfortable.
// CONSEQUENCE: a graph built from this recipe is a DEV_ VERIFICATION graph and is NOT PROMOTABLE under
// GNC-001 without a real judge. The forgeRoundTripOnly PASS is reachable only by a ZERO-bridge recipe
// such as fourWithHub-baseline, which is what the Phase 5 entry build used and what PASSED.
{
	"schemaVersion": "1.0.0",
	"recipeName": "fourWithHubFourBridges",
	"kind": "dev",
	"description": "The four certified standards with the CEDS hub, plus the four non-colliding bridge plugins (SIF standard-declared, Ed-Fi crosswalk and derived, PESC property-tier derived) — the Phase 5 verification graph.",
	"standards": [
		{ "token": "ceds", "version": "current" },
		{ "token": "edfi", "version": "current" },
		{ "token": "pesc260805", "version": "current" },
		{ "token": "sif", "version": "current" }
	],
	"hubs": [
		{ "standard": "ceds" }
	],
	"bridges": [
		{ "source": "sif", "hub": "ceds", "bridge": "sifCedsStandardPlugin", "dependencies": ["sif", "ceds"] },
		{ "source": "edfi", "hub": "ceds", "bridge": "edfiCedsCrosswalkPlugin", "dependencies": ["edfi", "ceds"] },
		{ "source": "edfi", "hub": "ceds", "bridge": "edfiCedsDerivedPlugin", "dependencies": ["edfi", "ceds"] },
		{ "source": "pesc260805", "hub": "ceds", "bridge": "pescCedsDerivedPlugin", "dependencies": ["pesc260805", "ceds"] }
	],
	"roundTripStage": true
}
